    "tolerance_cost_curve": "Going from ±0.1mm to ±0.01mm on a feature typically multiplies inspection time, adds fixturing, and can require multiple passes. Specify tight tolerance only where function demands it.",
    "anodize_growth": "Type II anodize grows roughly half its thickness outward (a 25um layer adds ~12um to the surface). Type III hardcoat is thicker and will visibly shrink tapped holes unless masked.",
